# Build context for the admin image.
#
# The context is ALLOWLISTED: `**` excludes everything, and then each
# thing the image needs is re-included. That is deliberate — the
# repository root is 1.1 GB of game assets, and an image that carries
# them is slow to build and leaks content.
#
# The console's modules and its static UI are re-included as
# DIRECTORIES, not one line per file. With one line per file, adding a
# module meant remembering to add a line HERE as well as to the
# Dockerfile, and forgetting either one ships an image that cannot
# start:
#
#   - the Dockerfile copies it but the allowlist does not → the build
#     fails with a checksum error;
#   - neither list mentions it → the build succeeds, the image is
#     missing the module, and the container dies with
#     ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
#
# One directory re-include means a new module is in the image because
# it exists, not because somebody remembered. See the registry's
# .dockerignore for the same rule and the incident behind it.
**
!services/admin/Dockerfile.admin
!services/admin/package.json
!services/admin/service.mjs
!services/admin/adminctl.mjs
!services/admin/lib/
!services/admin/public/
